<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_naturesblessing.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nature's Grace</span></a>, this Mastery is especially helpful because it will always occur with your eclipse.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Balance Druid Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>When deciding which trinket to go for, there are a couple of things that need to be taken into consideration. The first one is Hit, there is a lot of Hit on gear in T15 and we can therefore struggle to make space for Wushoolay's Final Choice. If we can't pick up Wushoolay's Final Choice, you will want to know roughly how much Crit you have. Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance scales its proc chance with your Crit, at 35% or higher Crit it procs more than Breath of the Hydra, and becomes your overall better choice.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96558/unerring-vision-of-lei-shen">
<img alt="Unerring Vision of Lei Shen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_hunter_focusedaim.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unerring Vision of Lei Shen</span></a> is incredibly strong for Balance Druid. It will however require actively tracking when it procs to take advantage of. When it procs, any DoT you can apply within a 4 second window will have 100% Crit until the DoT expires. Many players might find this challenging to play with, especially when trying to pay attention to the raid and its mechanics, so you might want to consider another trinket if you do not feel comfortable with getting off at least 2 DoTs every time this procs.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96413/wushoolays-final-choice">
<img alt="Wushoolay's Final Choice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_chainlightning.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wushoolay's Final Choice</span></a> is our second option for trinkets in Phase 3. It is a very strong trinket, but we are facing the issue of too much Hit in phase 3. In full BiS, we can simply not run this without going above the Hit cap. When not near BiS, if this one is available it's a very strong choice.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96516/cha-yes-essence-of-brilliance">
<img alt="Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_mindsooth.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance</span></a> is another option in Phase 3. This one is more gear reliant, as its proc chance is directly affected by how much Crit we have. This is the weakest trinket until you start getting a lot of gear, where it ends up being BiS.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96455/breath-of-the-hydra">
<img alt="Breath of the Hydra" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_mindflay.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Breath of the Hydra</span></a> is another option in Phase 3. It's very similar to Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance, but without Crit scaling, allowing it to be stronger early on and fall behind later.</div></li></ul>
