<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Balance Druids</span></h2>Nearly every profession in Mists of Pandaria provides a decent boost to your characters damage output. However, a few stand out for giving a bit of an extra boost.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Balance Druid</h4>Engineering brings several gadgets and tools that can be helpful in your adventures. <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87215/wormhole-generator-pandaria">
<img alt="Wormhole Generator: Pandaria" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/sha_spell_fire_felfirenova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wormhole Generator: Pandaria</span></a> will help you get around Pandaria more quickly. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=49040/jeeves">
<img alt="Jeeves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_mimiron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jeeves</span></a> allowing you to repair from anywhere without having to go back to a town. In addition, it provides the highest DPS boost out of any profession, from <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a>.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Balance Druid</h4>While you won't be equipping the things you craft with Tailoring, you will certainly benefit from <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142173/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a>, an embroidery unique to Tailors. The enchant will provide a chance to gain a large Intellect boost when casting spells. This is generally the highest-DPS profession for casters.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Balance Druid</h4>Blacksmithing isn't a profession to choose for crafting gear you would use, but rather for the benefits of two extra gem slots. Blacksmithing brings with it the now additional sockets we have come to expect, with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55628/socket-bracer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_socketedbracer.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Bracer</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55641/socket-gloves">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_addsocketglove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a>, giving a flexible stat choice that can be very strong. Especially with gems in Mists of Pandaria providing twice as much in secondary stats, Blacksmithing can help you reach your secondary stat caps.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Balance Druids</span></h3>Crafted items are no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Leatherworker, you can equip anything Leatherworkers craft. There are two crafted items in Tier 15 that we will be looking at. Both require <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94289/haunting-spirit">
<img alt="Haunting Spirit" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_envelopingshadows.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunting Spirit</span></a> which can only be obtained from disenchanting raid loot from Throne of Thunder. This may result in the items being very expensive early on.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94274/spirit-keeper-helm">
<img alt="Spirit Keeper Helm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_leather_raidmonk_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirit Keeper Helm</span></a> is an item made by Leatherworkers. It can be used as our offpiece until we get an item from heroic raiding, it does have Mastery so if you have any other similar item level offpieces they will likely be better.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94273/spirit-keeper-footguards">
<img alt="Spirit Keeper Footguards" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_leather_raidmonk_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirit Keeper Footguards</span></a> is an item made by Leatherworkers. It is better than Pre-BiS options, but weaker than raid options.</div></li></ul>
